  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1130 PM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nSouthwesterly flow aloft and lingering low- to mid-level\ndeformation are progged to be in place near our region on Sunday.\nWe could also see favorable alignment of the right entrance \nregion of the upper-level jet, at least briefly, but these\nfeatures have varying placement depending on individual model \nsolutions. These forcing considerations will help bring additional rain\nshowers to the area, best chances are across the southeast half \nof Middle Tennessee. Finally, a prominent northern stream \ndisturbance and associated reinforcing cold front is expected to \narrive Monday morning. This will bring a notably cooler, drier \nairmass that is forecast to stick around for much of next week. \nLows into the low 40s to low 50s are expected, though the dry \nairmass will allow for efficient afternoon warming as well; into \nthe 80s west of the Plateau by mid week.",
